qrenderdoc: Build with Qt6 as well as Qt5

Qt6 removed a long list of what qrenderdoc uses: QtX11Extras and QX11Info,
QRegExp, QDesktopWidget, QTextCodec, Qt::AA_X11InitThreads,
QLayout::setMargin and margin, QStyleOption::init, QPalette::foreground,
QPalette::Foreground and Background, QStyle::PE_IndicatorViewItemCheck,
QPainter::drawRoundRect and HighQualityAntialiasing, QFontMetrics::width,
QWheelEvent::delta, pos, x and orientation, QTime::start and elapsed,
QString::null and midRef, QModelIndex::child, QSet and QVector::toList,
QMetaType::registerComparators, QComboBox::setAutoCompletion,
QAbstractItemView::viewOptions, QSortFilterProxyModel::setFilterRegExp,
Qt::MidButton, Qt::ImMicroFocus, QVariant's relational operators and the
QString::SplitBehavior flags. It also made QVector an alias of QList,
turned QNetworkReply::error into a getter with errorOccurred as the
signal, made QLabel::pixmap return by value, QTimer::QPrivateSignal and
the event copy constructors inaccessible, changed QWidget::enterEvent to
take a QEnterEvent, and stopped converting 0 to any QFlags or NULL to
QPointer.

Port each of those, keeping the Qt5 spelling wherever the replacement is
newer than the Qt 5.6 this still builds against. QTextCodec is the one
exception: rather than rewrite scintilla's conversion layer, take it from
the Qt5Compat module that Qt ships for exactly this.

Qt6 also ignores a CONFIG request below c++17, so qrenderdoc.pro's
"CONFIG += c++14" left the standard up to the compiler's default. That is
gnu++20 with GCC 16, where the replay API structs that declare a
defaulted default constructor are no longer aggregates and the returns
that brace-initialise them stop compiling. Ask for c++17 with Qt6.

Finally, Qt6 gave QString an operator+=(QUtf8StringView) and an rvalue
operator+, which an rdcstr or rdcinflexiblestr converts to just as
readily as it does to QString, so appending or concatenating one became
ambiguous; exact-match operators settle it.

